g  about strategy here we're talking about  right and wrong we're talking about a  congressional duty to do what it is that  they're supposed to do given the  circumstances and the evidence that we  have but there are also some interesting  strategy articles being released related  to impeachment one example is from  Republican strategist Cheri Jacobus who  argues that impeachment will actually  help Democrats now we'll get at the end  of the show today today's voicemail is  from an angry trumpet  who is sort of begging for Democrats to  try to impeach Trump Trump believing  that this will just help Trump get  reelected in 2020 that's one perspective  what sherry Jacobus is pointing out is  that most Americans many Americans a  plurality of Americans whatever phrase  you want to apply to it don't have any  idea what's in the molar report in other  words most people have lives most people  aren't watching long congressional  hearings even if the Michael Cohen  congressional hearing had record ratings  for such a hearing the molar report is  450 pages and to the extent that people  see a news story about it or  unfortunately get their impressions of  what's in the molar report from the bar  letter which is a complete sort of miss  miss characterization of what's in the  molar report that if you actually start  debate on impeachment and move forward  on impeachment even if it doesn't  succeed at removing the president it  will inform people about the content of  the Moller report it will inform people  who have no idea what is actually going  on what it is that is being debated and  that has taken place and that in the  long run it will actually help Democrats  and hurt Donald Trump as we approach the  2020 election now should Democrats take  advice from a Republican strategist  maybe not  you also have Harvard Law Professor  Lawrence tribe who is for sure a  partisan actor but he is someone who  knows a lot about impeachment who says  at this point in time Donald Trump is  impeachable and by that he means  actually removable by a Senate vote on  the basis of impeachment proceedings  started by the house so the last five  days we've seen a very decided shift  here you've seen more and more Democrats  sort of abandoning the Nancy Pelosi  perspective of we shouldn't bother with  him with impeachment Trump's not worth  impeachment whatever other phraseology  she's applied to this since March you've  seen more and more momentum build  Democrats part ways with Nancy Pelosi  and what's clear at this point in time  without knowing exactly how this is  going to play out is that the discussion  about impeachment is not disappearing  next week and it's not disappearing next  month and  it's gone beyond the issue of political  strategy which I still believe to be  legitimate to one simply of given the  facts what is supposed to be Congress's  role in adjudicating the actions of the  President of the United States it's time  to start a floor debate on impeachment  and at that point in time once that has  happened Congress can decide do we want  to actually move forward with articles  of impeachment do we want to move  forward with censure of the president or  after this debate have we determined  that we're not going to go any further  that should be the immediate next step  and it goes well beyond political  strategy at this point in time today the  David Pakman show was made possible in  part by nord VPN which is a tool that  i've been using on my computer and my  phone to protect my privacy online and  to keep my personal data safe because it  allows you to change your device's IP  address making you totally anonymous on  the internet and Nord VPN is giving  everybody in our audience a 75% discount  on a three-year subscription this comes  out to less than three bucks a month  plus a whole month free when you go to  Nordby pn comm slash david pakman and  use the coupon code david pakman all one  word we know that the david pakman show  ha